    "ls|LS16_S17_U_113": " \n \n \n \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*113 \n FOR ANSWER ON 11/02/2019 \n \nSTEEL EXPORT \n \n*113. SHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM: \n \nWill the Minister of STEEL be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the quantity of steel being exported  and the revenue earned therefrom during  \neach of the last three years and the current year, country-wise; \n \n(b) whether the export oriented policy  of steel is the primary cause for escalation  \nof steel prices in the domestic market; and \n \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the  corrective measures taken/prop osed to be  \ntaken by the Government to bring down the prices? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STEEL     (SHRI CHAUDHARY BIRENDER SINGH) \n \n(a)to(c):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the Lok Sabha. \n \n******** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (C) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *113 FOR ANSWER ON 11/02/2019 TABLED \nBY SHRI GODSE HEMANT TUKARAM, MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING \n“STEEL EXPORT” \n \n(a) ��������������������������������������������������������������������for both quantity and value wise during last \nthree years and current year is given in the table 1 below:- \n \nTable 1: India’s export of Iron and Steel (quantity and value wise)  \n    Quantity in million tonnes Value in US$ billion \nCh Description 2015-\n16 \n2016-\n17 \n2017-\n18 \nApril-\nNov. \n2017-\n18 \nApril-\nNov. \n2018-\n19 \n2015-\n16 \n2016-\n17 \n2017-\n18 \nApril-\nNov. \n2017-\n18 \nApril-\nNov. \n2018-\n19 \n72 Iron and \nSteel 7.6 14.0 15.9 10.7 8.0 5.5 8.7 11.2 7.4 6.5 \nSource: DGCI&S \n \n����������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������both quantity \nand value wise during last three years and current year is given in the table 2 below:- \n \nTable 2: India’s export of Iron and steel (Ch 72) – top 20 countries \n(Value in US$ million) \n Countries 2015-16 2016-2017 2017-2018  A