    "ls|LS16_S17_U_125": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \n \nLOK SABHA \n \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 125 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \n \nSKILL TRAINING UNDER PMKVY \n \n \n125. SHRI TEJ PRATAP SINGH YADAV: \nSHRI L.R. SHIVARAME GOWDA: \nSHRIMATI ANJU BALA: \n \n \nWill the MINISTER of SKILL DEVELOPMENT and ENTREPRE NEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state : \n \n(a) whether the Government is implementing Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas \nYojana (PMKVY) skill training of the youth and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(b) the funds allocated, released and utilised vis-a-vis target fixed and achieved \nalong with the number of persons benefited and empl oyed under PMKVY since its \ninception till date, year and State/UT-wise; \n \n(c) whether the Government has conducted any survey  on the benefit accrued to \nthe youth as a result of launch of the PMKVY and if so, the details thereof; \n \n(d) whether any grievance redressal system/online p ortal is in place to address \ngrievances relating to implementation of the scheme  and if so, the details thereof; \nand \n \n(e) whether a Skill Development Management System ( SDMS) is proposed to be \nput in place to verify and record details of all tr aining centres and if so, the details \nthereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI ANANTKUMAR HEGDE) \n \n(a) and (b) Under Skill India Mission, Ministry of Skill Development and \nEntrepreneurship is implementing a flagship scheme known as Pradhan Mantri \nKaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) 2016-20 with an object ive to provide skilling to one \ncrore people under Short Term Training (STT), Recog nition of Prior Learning (RPL) \nand Special Project (SP) across the country for fou r years i.e. 2016-2020 with an \noutlay of 12,000 crore. \n \nPMKVY 2016-20 has two components known as Centrally  Sponsored \nCentrally Managed (CSCM) being implemented by Natio nal Skill Development \nCorporation (NSDC) and Centrally Sponsored State Ma naged (CSSM) being \nimplemented by State Skill Development Missions of the States/ UTs popularly \nknown as State- Engagement Component of PMKVY (2016-20). \n \nUnder CSCM component of PMKVY 2016-20, there is no provision of State-\nwise funds allocation. As on 24.01.2019, an amount of Rs. 550 Cr., Rs. 1132.48 Cr. \nand Rs. 1455.16 Cr. has been disbursed to implement ing agency (i.e. NSDC) during \nFY 2016-17, FY 2017-18 and FY 2018-19, respectively . Further, under CSSM \n\ncomponent of PMKVY 2016-20, 25% of the funds and co rresponding physical targets \nof PMKVY 2016-20 has been allocated to the States f or the implementation of \nscheme through State Skill Development Missions. Un der this component, after \nevaluation of proposal received from of 36 States/U Ts, Ministry has given in-principle \napproval of a total target of 20.18 lakh candidates  and corresponding financial \nallocation of Rs. 3,050 Cr. for FY 2016-20. Out of which, as on 24.01.2019, funds \namounting to Rs. 759.93 Cr. has been already disbur sed to State Governments / \nSSDMs. The State-wise details of in-principle appro ved physical, and financial \nallocation and funds disbursed under CSSM component  of PMKVY 2016-20 are \ngiven at Annexure-I. \n \nUnder PMKVY 2016-20, as on 24.01.2019, 37.32 lakh ( appx.) candidates \nhave been trained under STT (25.25 lakh), RPL (11.2 7 lakh) and Special Project (0.8 \nlakh) in the country. Under PMKVY 2016-20 scheme, p lacement tracking is \nmandatory. The placement data is reported within 90  days of certification of trained \ncandidate. As per data reported on SDMS, as on 24.0 1.2019, 21.03 lakh candidates \nare certified under STT and SPs of PMKVY 2016-20. T he number of candidates \ncertified under STT and SPs of PMKVY 90 days prior i.e. 26.10.2018 is 19.39 lakh. \nOut of these candidates, as on 24.01.2019, 10.64 la kh candidates have been placed \nin various sectors across the country. The State-wi se number of candidates enrolled, \ntrained, assessed, certified and placed under PMKVY  2016-20, as on 24.01.2019, \nare given at Annexure II . \n \n(c) NSDC, an implementing agency of PMKVY, has alre ady engaged a third party \nagency Sambodhi Research and Communications Pvt. Lt d. to conduct the impact \nevaluation of on-going Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana 2016-20.  \n \n(d) NSDC has put in place a specific grievance emai l address on its portal and a \ndedicated team takes care of the grievances receive d through online system, \ngrievance portal and via RTIs. Further, under the s cheme, PMKVY 2016-20 \nMonitoring Committee review and formulate framework  on the critical cases related \nto monitoring issues of the stakeholders. Also, the  Committee has formulated penalty \ngrid (approved by Steering Committee for PMKVY) for  taking action against erring / \nnon compliant training centres / stakeholders. Base d on the penalty grid, National \nSkill Development Corporation (NSDC) has suspended training centers for \nnoncompliance of PMKVY 2016-20 guidelines on multip le parameters and \nperiodically publishes the list on PMKVY official website. \n \n(e) Skill Development Management System (SDMS) is a lready operational to \ncapture life cycle of candidates under the scheme. The existing feature includes \ncapturing of complete information of candidates, tr aining providers, training centres, \nand capturing process related details such enrolmen t, training, assessment, result, \ncertification and bank details for reward money disbursement. \n  \n\nAnnexure I \n \nThe State-wise details of in-principle approved phy sical and financial allocation and \nfunds disbursed, as on 24.01.2019, under CSSM compo nent of PMKVY 2016-20 are \ngiven below: \n \nS. \nNo.  \nState Name Physical Targets \nApproval (2016-20) \nFunds Approved \n(2016-20) \nFunds Released \nby MSDE \n1. A & N Islands 4,108  6,32,51,698  2,10,78,767  \n2. Andhra Pradesh 64,608  94,74,11,712  28,84,26,464  \n3. Arunachal Pradesh 29,510  43,27,34,640  7,21,32,216  \n4. Assam 47,258  72,76,40,878  36,95,32,800  \n5. Bihar 89,664  1,38,05,74,540  36,81,62,449  \n6. Chandigarh 10,288  15,84,06,394  6,15,88,800  \n7. Chhattisgarh 48,532  71,16,73,248  13,19,76,000  \n8. Dadra & Nagar Haveli 4,000  6,15,88,800  1,10,85,984  \n9. Daman & Diu 4,000  6,15,88,800  3,00,24,540  \n10. Delhi 81,000  1,24,71,73,200  15,39,72,000  \n11. Goa  46,951  72,29,13,937  10,70,25,937  \n12. Gujarat 77,824  1,19,82,71,693  35,94,93,826  \n13. Haryana 56,036  86,27,97,499  21,56,99,375  \n14. Himachal Pradesh 49,499  76,21,46,003  21,55,60,800  \n15. Jammu & Kashmir 47,302  72,83,18,354  22,94,18,280  \n16. Jharkhand 57,668  88,79,25,730  29,59,64,978  \n17. Karnataka 94,164  1,38,08,20,896  21,43,95,135  \n18. Kerala 71,450  1,10,01,29,940  22,00,25,988  \n19. Lakshwadeep 2,400  3,69,53,280  1,23,17,760  \n20. Madhya Pradesh 84,058  1,23,26,26,512  21,46,66,296  \n21. Maharashtra 1,67,127  2,57,32,87,845  85,77,62,615  \n22. Manipur 32,472  49,99,77,879  24,99,88,939  \n23. Meghalaya 33,642  51,79,92,602  12,77,96,760  \n24. Mizoram 36,671  56,46,30,721  10,88,73,601  \n25. Nagaland 33,021  50,84,30,941  16,94,76,980  \n26. Odisha 58,046  89,37,45,871  27,71,49,600  \n27. Puducherry 10,619  15,57,17,016  2,59,55,280  \n28. Punjab 55,028  80,69,30,592  26,39,52,000  \n29. Rajasthan 64,526  94,62,15,130  14,19,35,789  \n30. Sikkim 4,900  7,54,46,280  2,00,16,360  \n31. Tamil Nadu 1,40,880  2,06,58,64,320  34,43,10,720  \n32. Telangana 59,611  91,78,42,489  22,94,64,472  \n33. Tripura 36,875  54,07,35,000  8,37,68,100  \n34. Uttar Pradesh 1,42,552  2,09,04,00,000  52,26,00,000  \n35. Uttarakhand 48,236  74,26,99,339  20,32,43,040  \n36. West Bengal 1,23,550  1,90,23,24,060  38,04,64,812  \nGrand Total 20,18,076  30,50,71,87,839  7,59,93,07,463  \n \n  \n\nAnnexure II \n \nThe State-wise number of candidates enrolled, train ed, assessed, certified and \nplaced under PMKVY 2016-