    "ls|LS16_S17_U_157": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.†157 \nANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF TOURIST PLACES IN MADHYA PRADESH AND \nCHHATTISGARH \n \n†157. SHRI UDAY PRATAP SINGH:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has provided any financial assistance \nto Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh for development of \nexisting and new tourist places and organizing festivals during \nthe last three years and the current year;  \n(b)  if so, the details thereof, year-wise;  \n(c)  the year -wise details of the steps taken or schemes \nformulated by the Government for promotion of tourist places \nlocated in Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh for \nattracting/encouraging tourists;  \n(d)  the details of the proposals received from Madhya Pradesh and \nChhattisgarh in this regard; and  \n(e)  the reasons for pendency of the proposals received? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SHRI K.J. ALPHONS) \n \n(a) to (e): Ministry of Tourism provides Central Financial \nAssistance to State Governments/Union Territory Administrations \nincluding the States of Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh under its \nvarious Schemes: \n \ni) Swadesh Darshan Scheme for development of theme based \ntourism circuits. \n\nii) National Mission on Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and Spiritual, \nHeritage Augmentation Drive (PRASHAD) Scheme for \nintegrated development of identified pilgrimage and heritage \ndestinations.  \niii) Financial Assistance to State Government/Union Territory \nAdministrations for Organizing Fair and Festivals and Tourism \nrelated Events. \n \n Ministry of Tourism promotes various tourism sites and \nproducts of different States/Union Territories including those in the \nStates of Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh in the domestic and \ninternational markets through media campaigns and activities \nundertaken by Indiatourism domestic and overseas offices. \n \n Submission of project proposals by the State Governments/UT \nAdministrations under the above schemes is a continuous process. \nThe projects for development are identif ied in consultation with the \nState Governments/UT Administrations and are sanctioned subject \nto availability of funds, submission of suitable detailed project \nreports, adherence to scheme guidelines and utilization of funds \nreleased earlier. \n \n Details of p rojects sanctioned to the State Governments of \nMadhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh under the above schemes during \nthe last three years and current year is given at Annexure. \n \n******** \n\nANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUE STION NO.†157  ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \nREGARDING DEVELOPMENT OF TOURIST PLACES IN MADHYA \nPRADESH AND CHHATTISGARH. \n \nSwadesh Darshan Scheme       (Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState/UT Name of \nthe \nCircuit \nName of the \nProject \nAmt. \nSanctioned \nAmt. \nReleased \nYear 2015-16 \n1. Madhya \nPradesh \nWildlife \nCircuit \nDevelopment \nof Wildlife \nCircuit at \nPanna- \nMukundpur- \nSanjay- Dubri-\nBandhavgarh- \nKanha- Mukki- \nPench in \nMadhya \nPradesh. \n92.22 73.78 \n2. Chhattisgarh Tribal \nCircuit \nDevelopment \nof Tribal \nTourism \nCircuit in \nJashpur- \nKunkuri- \nMainpat- \nAmbikapur- \nMaheshpur -\nRatanpur- \nKurdar-\nSarodadadar- \nGangrel- \nKondagaon– \nNathiya \nNawagaon- \nJagdalpur- \nChitrakoot- \n99.21 73.29 \n\nTirthgarh in \nChhattisgarh.                                                                                     \nYear 2016-17   \n3. Madhya \nPradesh \nBuddhist \nCircuit \nDevelopment \nof Buddhist \nCircuit in \nSanchi-Satna-\nRewa-\nMandsaur-\nDhar in \nMadhya \nPradesh. \n74.94 37.47 \n4. Madhya \nPradesh \nHeritage \ncircuit \nDevelopment \nof Heritage \nCircuit \n(Gwalior – \nOrchha – \nKhajuraho – \nChanderi – \nBhimbetka – \nMandu) \nMadhya \nPradesh \n99.77 \n \n49.89 \n \nYear 2017-18 \n5. Madhya \nPradesh \nEco \nCircuit \nDevelopment \nof \nGandhisagar \nDam- \nMandleshwar \nDam- \nOmkareshwar \nDam- Indira \nSagar Dam - \nTawa Dam - \nBargi Dam - \nBheda Ghat - \nBansagar \nDam- Ken \nRiver under \nEco circuit \ntheme of \n99.62 73.56 \n\nSwadesh \nDarshan \nScheme \n \nPRASHAD Scheme        (Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState Name of the Project Project \nCost \nAmt. \nRelease\nd \nYear 2017-18  \n1 MADHYA \nPRADESH \nDevelopment of \nOmkareshwar \n40.67 18.76 \n \nFinancial Assistance to State Government/Un ion Territory \nAdministrations for Organizing Fair and Festivals and Tourism \nrelated Events \n(Rs. in Lakh) \nName of \nState \nYear Name of the festival Amt. \nSanctioned \nAmt. \nReleased \nChhattisgarh  2015-16  \nto \n2017-18 \n NIL  -- -- \n2018-19 (i) Bastar Dushera \nLokstav \n(ii) Rajim Kumbh \nMahotsav \n(iii)Bhoramdeo \nfestival  \n25.00 25.00 \nMadhya \nPradesh \n2015-16 (i) Sharad Utsav, \nBhedaghat \n(ii) Mandu Utsav \n(iii)Pachmarhi \nUtsav, Pachmarhi \n19.00 19.00 \n2016-17 (i)  Pachmarhi \nUtsav, Pachmarhi \n(ii) Jal Mahotsav, \nHanuwantiya  \n(iii)World Tourism \nDay Celebration, \n2016  \n(iv)Sharad Utsav, \nBhedaghat \n42.00 42.00 \n\n(Jabalpur)  \n(v) Mandu Utsav - \n2016 \n 2017-18 (i) Pachmarhi Utsav, \nPachmarhi \n(ii) Jal Mahotsav, \nHanuwantia  \n(iii)Khajuraho Dance \nFestival \n50.00 50.00 \n2018-19 (i) Panchmari Utsav \n(ii) Jal Mahotsav  \n(iii)Khajuraho Dance \nFestival  \n50.00 50.00 \n \n********* \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_158": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n�\nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.158 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 13.02.2019 \n \nSTOPPAGE OF TRAINS \n \n��*158.  SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR: \n \n        Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n(a)  whether  a verbal announcement was made for the stoppage of \ntrains at Rampur 12 Km. from Daniyawa to Bihar Shariff railway \nline in Nalanda district of Bihar; \n(b) whether neither the tickets are issued nor the passenger facilities \nare available at Rampur as the Gov ernment has not issued orders \nregarding this; \n(c)    if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(d) the steps being taken by the Government to make the said \nstoppage official/formal and provide passenger facilities at this \nstation through official/formal orders? \n \nANSWER \n   \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS, COAL, FINANCE AND CORPORATE AFFAIRS \n \n \n (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n   \n(a) to (d): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n***** \n \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 158 BY SHRI KAUSHALENDRA KUMAR  TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 13.02.2019 REGARDING STOPPAGE OF \nTRAINS \n \n(a) to (d): There is no such station/halt ������������ ��Rampur�� on Daniyawan \n(DHWN) - Bihar Sharif (BEHS) section in Danapur division, at present.   \n        However, a proposal for opening of a passenger halt at Rampur village \nwas examined but not found justified due to anticipated meagre sale of \ntickets. Moreover, two adjacent halts i.e. Rukhai and Lachhubigha are \npresently operational, one at a distance of only 2.2 Kms fr om the proposed \nlocation at Rampur village on each end. Opening of another halt at such \nclose proximity is not justified due to operational and commercial reasons. \n***** ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_159": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 159 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nTechnical Education Institutions \n \n†159. SHRI ADHALRAO PATIL SHIVAJIRAO:  \nSHRI ANANDRAO ADSUL:  \nDR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE:  \nSHRI DHARMENDRA YADAV:  \nSHRI VINAYAK BHAURAO RAUT: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Government has approved an ambitious scheme of 2660 crore rupees with \nassistance from the World Bank with a view to improving quality of technical education \ninstitutions in the States;  \n(b) if so, the details in this regard along with the main features of the said scheme; \n(c) the details of the technical education in stitutions selected under the said scheme; \n(d) the criteria laid down for selection of the said technical education institutions; and \n(e) whether the work has started under the said scheme and if so, the details thereof in this \nregard and if not, the present status thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n \n (DR. SATYA PAL SINGH)  \n \n \n(a) to (e):    The Govt. of India has approv ed the third phase of Technical Education Quality \nImprovement Programme (TEQIP-III), with assistance from the World Bank, for improving the \noverall quality of Technical Education in 19 focus states (7 low income states, 3 hill states, 8 \nnorth eastern region states and Union Territory of Andaman & Nicobar Islands) with an outlay of \nRs. 2660 crore.  The programme has commenced from April 2017 with implementation period of \n3 years. The main objective of the project is to enhance quality and equity in selected engineering \neducation institutes and improve the efficiency of the engineering education system in Focus \nStates. The details regarding objective of TEQ IP-III, main features, technical education \ninstitutions selected, criteria of selection of institu tes, present status of scheme may be seen at \nhttp://mhrd.gov.in/sites/upload_files/mhrd/files/Details_regarding_scheme_TEQIP-III.pdf. \n \n***** \n\t",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_16": "��������� �\n������������������������� �\n���������������������������� �\n��\n������������������������������������������\n��\n�������������������\n��\n����������������������������������������������� ������������������������������� �� ��������������������������\n����������������������\n��\n����� � ������� ���� ����������� ��� �������� ��� ������ ��� ������� ���� ���������� ��� ������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������\n���� ������������������������������\n����� ����������������������������������������������� ������������������������������� ����\n������� ���������� ���� ���� ������ ���� ���������� ������������������� ��� ���������� �����\n����������������������������������������������\n����� ���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���������������\n�\n������ �\n�\n�������������������������������������������������������\n������ ���\n�\n������������ ���� ����������� ���� ����� ������� ���������� �������� ��� ������ ������� ��������\n���������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n���� �������� ��� ����� ��� ��� ���������� ���������� ���� �������� �������� ��� ���� ���������������\n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������ �� ���� ������� ���� ������� �������� ��� ���� ������������������������ ��� ���� �����������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n��������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������\n�������������������\n�",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_160": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.160 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nINDUSTRIAL TRAINING INSTITUTES \n \n160: SHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM \n \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be pleased to \nstate: \n(a) the details of the Industrial Training Institut es (ITIs) functioning in the country at present \nalong with the skill trades being taught in these institutes, State/UT-wise including Gujarat; \n \n(b) the number of students being learned in these i nstitutes and the existing vacancies in \nvarious categories along with the plan to fill up these vacancies, State/UT-wise including Gujarat; \n \n(c) whether the Government proposes to set up new I TIs in the country and if so, the details \nthereof, State/phase-wise; \n \n(d) whether the Government has prepared any fresh p lan to upgrade ITIs in the country and if \nso, the details thereof including integration of ITIs with Skill Development Programmes; and \n \n(e) the details of the amount spent on improvement of ITIs in the country during each of the last \nthree years, State-wise including Gujarat? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI ANANTKUMAR HEGDE) \n(a) There are 15044 Industrial Training Institutes (ITI s) functioning in the country, affiliated with \nNational Council of Vocational Training. The State/ UT wise list of ITIs are attached at Annexure I . \n \n(b) Total number of students undergoing training in 150 44 ITIs (Annexure-I)  is 2643443. To fill \nup the vacant seats and for optimum utilization of infrastructure, respective State Directorate (S/D) \nhave their own strategy.  \n \n(c) \nVocational Training is a concurrent subject under t he Constitution wherein the                        \nCentral Government is entrusted with the responsibi lity of formulation of policy, laying down \ntraining standards, norms examination and certifica tion. New ITIs (Govt./ Pvt.) are setup under \nadministrative control of concerned State Directorate/Union Territory. DGT has been taking prompt \naction on receipt of proposal from the State/ UT for opening of new ITIs. \n \n(d) Directorate General of Training under Ministry of S kill Development and Entrepreneurship \nhas been making continuous efforts to improve the q uality of training, offered by the ITIs through \nthe country, which includes: \n1. Prescribed new Affiliation Norms for ITIs with a fo cus on improvement of quality of \nTraining. \n2. Regular inspection of ITIs and de-affiliation of IT Is to weed out ITIs not conforming to the \nNCVT norms & standards.  \n3. ISO 29990 Certification of ITIs to raise the overall quality and standards. \n4. Grading of ITIs to evaluate their performance. \n5. Introduction of new trades and removal of obsolete trades for industry relevance. \n\n6. Regular up-gradation of training content of ITI curriculum as per industrial requirement \n7. Aligning the courses under Craftsman Training Schem e (CTS) to National Skills \nQualification Framework (NQSF)  \n8. Implementation of ‘Dual System of Training’ in ITIs leading to better ITI- Industry linkage. \n9. Training and re-training of ITI Instructors. \n10. Up gradation of infrastructure of ITIs through following centrally funded schemes: \ni. World Bank assisted Vocational Training Improvem ent Project (VTIP). \nii. Up-gradation of 1396 Government ITIs through PP P. \niii. Up-gradation of existing Government ITIs into Model ITIs. \n \n(e) Directorate General of Training, MoSDE has formulat ed following schemes to fund ITIs in \nvarious States for Skill Development: \n \n1. Enhancing Skill Development Infrastructure in North  Eastern States and Sikkim: The \nscheme inter-alia envisages up gradation of 22 exis ting ITIs by establishment of 3 new \ntrades in each ITI; supplementing deficient infrast ructure in 28 ITIs by constructing new \nboundary wall, new hostel along with supplementing old and obsolete tools and equipment \nfor 3 existing trades in each ITI. The details of c overage and fund released are at \nAnnexure II.  \n \n2. Up gradation of existing Government ITIs into Model  ITIs: Existing ITI in a State has been \nchosen for up gradation into Model ITI which is sup posed to evolve as an institution \nshowcasing best practices, efficient and high quali ty training delivery and sustainable and \neffective industry relationship.  Institute Managem ent Committee (IMC) society for each ITI \nwith chairperson from Industry is empowered to impl ement the scheme at ITI level. The \ndetails of fund released including Gujarat State are at Annexure III.  \n \n3. The World Bank assisted Vocational Training Improve ment Project (VTIP): The Vocational \nTraining Improvement Project (VTIP), interalia, env isages up gradation of 400 ITIs in 34 \nState Governments/UTs including NE States under the  project. Physical component \nconsisted of setting up of new classrooms, workshop s and modernization of tools, \nequipment and machinery, training of trainers and e nsuring improved learning environment. \nMost of the States have been able to complete the c reation of physical infrastructure. The \ndetails of fund released including Gujarat State are at Annexure IV . \n \n****** \n\n \nAnnexure-I \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply of part (a) of LSUQ No.160 on Industrial Training \nInstitutes raised by SHRIMATI POONAMBEN MAADAM for answer on 04.02.2019.  \n \nSTATE/UT WISE DETAILS \nITI COUNT AS ON DATED-28.12.2018 \nSl.No State/District ITI Count \n1 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 3 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 506 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 6 \n4 Assam 30 \n5 Bihar 1219 \n6 Chandigarh 2 \n7 Chhattisgarh 227 \n8 Dadra & Nagar Haveli 1 \n9 Daman & Diu 2 \n10 Delhi 59 \n11 Goa 15 \n12 Gujarat 418 \n13 Haryana 399 \n14 Himachal Pradesh 251 \n15 Jammu and Kashmir 38 \n16 Jharkhand 273 \n17 Karnataka 1543 \n18 Kerala 631 \n19 Lakshadweep