    "ls|LS16_S17_U_169": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n(DEPARTMENT OF COMMERCE) \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 169(H) \nTO BE ANSWERED ON  04th FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \n \nBOOSTING COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY SECTOR IN RAJASTHAN \n \n169(H). SHRI MANSHANKAR NINAMA: \nWill the Minister of COMMERCE & INDUSTRY (वाͨणÏय एवं उɮयोग मंğी ) be \npleased to state: \n(a) whether the Government is taking any measures to boost commerce and industry \nsector in Rajasthan;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof;  \n(c) whether the Government is aware that additional expenditure and time is spent on \nimport and export in absence of a port in Rajasthan which is a desert State; \n(d) if so, the steps taken/being taken by the Government in this regard; and \n(e) whether the Government of Rajasthan has sent any proposal to the Union \nGovernment in this regard and if so, the action taken by the Government in this \nregard so far? \n \nANSWER \n \nokf.kT; ,oa m|ksx ea=ky; esa jkT; ea=h ¼Jh lh- vkj- pkS/kjh½  \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF COMMERCE AND INDUSTRY  \n (SHRI C. R. CHAUDHARY)  \n \n(a) to  (e) : With an objective to ensure a continuous dialogue with all State Governments on \nmeasures for providing an International trade enabling environment in the State and to create a \nframework for making the States active partners in boosting India’s trade, a Council for Trade \nDevelopment and Promotion (CTDP) has been constituted (notified in July 2015) under the \nchairmanship of the Union Commerce and Industry Minister, in which the Trade & Commerce \nMinisters of all the states, including Rajasthan are members.  Regular annual meetings of the \nCouncil have been conducted to facilitate the States to articulate their views. \nFurther, key initiatives like ‘Make in India’, ‘Start-up India’ and ‘Ease of Doing \nBusiness’ have also been taken by the Government to facilitate industrial production and growth in \nthe States, including Rajasthan. \n \n           The Government has facilitated setting up of dry ports which help the exporters \nfrom land locked States and have so far accorded clearance to 7 proposals for setting up \nof Inland Container Depots in Rajasthan. No specific proposal from Government of \nRajasthan is presently pending with the Department. \n****** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_17": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.*17 \nANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nREVENUE GENERATED FROM TOURISM \n \n*17. SHRI DEVUSINH CHAUHAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  the average revenue generated and fore ign exchange earned from \ntourism during the last three years;  \n(b)  the details of the ongoing schemes for the development and \npromotion of tourism and the number of tourism infra structure \nprojects prioritised/ sanctioned during the above period, State/ UT -\nwise, particularly in Gujarat;  \n(c)  whether the Government has received proposals from various States \nfor the development and promotion of tourism and allocation of funds \ntherefor;  \n(d)  if so, the details thereof indicating the number of such proposals \nreceived and the number of projects sanctioned and funds allocated, \nState-wise; and  \n(e)  whether the Government proposes to increase allocation of funds for \ntourism infrastructure, promotion, publicity of tourist destinations \nand products in the domestic and international markets and if so, the \ndetails thereof? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SHRI K.J. ALPHONS) \n \n(a) to (e): A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n******** \n \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO LOK SABHA STARRED QUESTIO N NO. *17 \nANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 REGARDING REVENUE GENERATED FROM \nTOURISM  \n \n(a): The estimated foreign exchange earnings (FEEs) through tourism in \nIndia during 2015, 2016 and 2017 were Rs. 134844 crore, Rs.154146 crore \nand Rs.177874 crore, respectively. Min istry of Tourism does not compile \nthe information on revenue generated by tourism in the country. \n \n(b) to (d): Development and promotion of tourist destinations including \nidentification of places of tourist interest is primarily the responsibility of \nState Governments/ Union Territory (UT) Administrations. However, \nMinistry of Tourism provides Central Financial Assistance under its two \nflagship schemes namely ‘Swadesh Darshan (SD)’ and ‘National Mission on \nPilgrimage Rejuvenation and Spiritual, Heritage Aug mentation Drive \n(PRASHAD)’ for the development of tourism related infrastructure and \nfacilities to promote tourism in the country.  \n \nSubmission of projects by the State Governments/ Union Territories \nunder the schemes is a continuous process. The projects under the \nschemes are identified for development in consultation with the State \nGovernments/ UT Administrations and are sanctioned subject to \navailability of funds, submission of suitable detailed project reports, \nadherence to scheme guidelines and utilization of funds released earlier. \n  \nThe details of projects sanctioned to States / UTs including Gujarat \nunder SD and PRASHAD  schemes are given at Annexure - I and Annexure     \n- II respectively. \n \n (e): The Ministry of Tourism, Government of India, as part o f its on-going \nactivities, releases media campaigns in the print, electronic, online and \noutdoor media in the international and domestic markets to promote \nvarious tourism destinations and products of the country. The expenditure \non campaigns released in t he international and domestic markets is \nincurred from funds allocated under the heads of “Restructured Overseas \nPromotion and Publicity including Marketing Development Assistance \n(OPMD)” and “Domestic Promotion and Publicity including Hospitality \n(DPPH)” respectively.  \n \nThe Budget Estimate (BE) allocated for creation of tourism \ninfrastructure and promotion of tourism to different schemes of the \nMinistry during the last three years are as below: \n \n\n \n(Rs. in Crore) \nYear Swadesh \nDarshan \nPRASHAD OPMD DPPH  \n2016-17 706.35 100.00 300.00 110.00 \n2017-18 959.91 100.00 300.00 110.00 \n2018-19 1100.00 150.00 454.24 135.00 \n \n********** \n\n \nANNEXURE – I \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (b) to (d) OF LOK SABHA ST