    "ls|LS16_S17_U_191": "GOVERNMENT\tOF\tINDIA\t\nMINISTRY\tOF\tHUMAN\tRESOURCE\tDEVELOPMENT\t\nDEPARTMENT\tOF\tHIGHER\tEDUCATION\t\n\t\nLOK\tSABHA\t\nUNSTARRED\tQUESTION\tNO.\t191\t\nTO\tBE\tANSWERED\tON\t04.02.2019\t\n\t\nTechnical\tEducation\t\t\n\t\n†191.\tSHRI\tKUNWAR\tPUSHPENDRA\tSINGH\tCHANDEL:\t\n\t\nWill\tthe\tMinister\tof\tHUMAN\tRESOURCE\tDEVELOPMENT\tbe\tpleased\tto\tstate:\t\n\t\t\n(a)\t whether\tthe\tGovernment\thas\tapproved\ta\tnew\tambitious\tscheme\t to\timprove\tthe\tquality\t\nof\ttechnical\teducation\tinstitutions\tlocated\tin\tvarious\tStates;\t\t\n(b)\t if\tso,\tthe\tdetails\tthereof;\t\t\n( c ) \t w h e t h e r \tt h e \tG o v e r n m e n t \th a s \ta n y \tp l a n \tf o r \ti m p r o v e m e n t \ta n d \tq u al i t y \tu p g r a d a t i o n \to f \t\ntechnical\tinstitution\tlocated\tin\tBundelkhand;\tand\t\n(d)\t\t if\tso,\tthe\tdetails\tthereof?\t\nANSWER\t\n\t\nMINISTER\tOF\tSTATE\tIN\tTHE\tMINISTRY\tOF\tHUMAN\tRESOURCE\tDEVELOPMENT\t\n\t\n\t(DR.\tSATYA\tPAL\tSINGH)\t\t\n\t\n( a ) \tt o \t( d ) : \t\t\t\tT h e \tG o v t . \to f \tI n d i a \th a s \ta p p r o v e d \tt h e \tt h i r d \tp h a s e \to f \tT e c h n i c a l \tE d u c a t i o n \tQ u a l i t y \t\nImprovement\tProgramme\t(TEQIP‐III),\twith\tassistance\tfrom\tthe\tWor ld\tBank,\tfor\timproving\tthe\t\noverall\t quality\t of\t Technical\t Education\t in\t 19\t focus\t states\t (7\t low \ti n c o m e \ts t a t e s , \t3 \th i l l \ts t a t e s , \t8 \t\nnorth\teastern\tregion\tstates\tand\tUnion\tTerritory\tof\tAndaman\t&\tNi cobar\tIslands)\twith\tan\toutlay\t\nof\t Rs.\t 2660\t crore.\t The\t programme\t has\t commenced\t from\t April\t 2017\tand\t has\t implementation\t\nperiod\t of\t 3\t years.\t The\t main\t objective\t the\t project\t is\t to\t enhance\tq u a l i t y \ta n d \te q u i t y \ti n \ts e l e c t e d \t\nengineering\teducation\tinstitutes\tand\timprove\tthe\tefficiency\tof\tthe\tengineering\teducation\tsystem\t\nin\tFocus\tStates.\tThree\tGovt./Govt.\taided\tEngineering\tInstitutio ns\tfrom\tBundelkhand\thave\tbeen\t\nselected\tunder\tTEQIP‐III,\tthe\tdetails\tof\twhich\tare\tas\tfollows:\t\n\t\ni. Institute\tof\tEngineering\t&\tTechnology,\tBundelkhand\tUniversity,\tJhansi\t\nii. Bundelkhand\tInstitute\tof\tEngineering\t&\tTechnology,\tJhansi\t\niii. Rajkiya\tEngineering\tCollege,\tBanda\t\n\t\n*****\t\n\t",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_192": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 192  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019  \n \nHigher Education Regulator \n192. SHRI ASHOK SHANKARRAO CHAVAN:  \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state:  \n(a) whether the Government is working with NITI Aayog on a plan to bring technical as \nwell as non-technical institutions under the same umbrella;   \n(b) if so, the details thereof and the objectives behind the move; \n(c) whether this move will replace Union Grants Commission and All India Council of \nTechnical Education with a single higher education regulator;  \n(d) if so, the details thereof;  \n(e) whether earlier also many committees have recommended for a single higher \neducation regulator but not implemented;  \n(f) if so, the details thereof and the reasons for non-implementation of their \nrecommendations; and  \n(g) the time by which a single higher education regulator would be set up? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(DR. SATYA PAL SINGH) \n \n(a) to (d): At present, there is no decisive move by the Government and NITI Aayog to \nbring technical and non-technical institutions under the same umbrella.  \n \n(e) to (g): The National Knowledge Commission (2006) recommended for an independent \nregulatory authority for higher education and the Committee on Renovation and \nRejuvenation of Higher Education (Professor Yashpal Committee: 2009) advocated an \napex regulatory body by converging multiple regulatory agencies in the field of higher \neducation. Further, the University Grants Commission Review Committee  (Prof. Hari \n\nGautam Committee) in 2014 had recommended that the University Grants Commission \nshould be replaced by an apex institution entitled National Higher Education Authority.  \n \n The Higher Education and Research Bill, 2011 was introduced in the Parliament \nfor establishment of the National Commission for Higher Education and Research by \nsubsuming the roles of the University Grants Commission and some of the Statutory \nCouncils. The Bill was examined by the Department related Parliamentary Standing \nCommittee on Human Resource Development. Parliamentary Standing Committee had \nexpressed its concerns on certain provisions of the Bill. In view of the suggestions and \nrecommendations of the Parliamentary Standing Committee, the Government decided to \nwithdraw the Bill in 2014.   \n****** \n  \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_193": "LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 193 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nGas Distribution Facility \n \n193. SHRI PARVESH SAHIB SINGH: \n \nWill the Minister of PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS  पेट्रोलियम और प्राक ृ लिक गैस मंत्री be \npleased to state:  \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to provide clean fuel in every village and town in the \ncountry and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b) the details of the districts and villages in Delhi that have been provided with the gas \ndistribution facility during the last four years; and  \n(c) whether the Government proposes to provide the Gas distribution facility to the remaining  \ndistricts and villages in Delhi and if so, the details thereof along with list of those areas which are \nunder process for the extension of this facility? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF PETROLEUM AND NATURAL GAS (SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board (PNGRB) is the authority to grant authorization \nto the entities for the development of City Gas Distribution (CGD) network in Geographical \nAreas (GAs) as per PNGRB Act, 2006.  PNGRB identifies GAs for authorizing the development \nof CGD ne twork in synchronization with the development of natural gas pipeline connectivity/ \nnatural gas availability.   With the completion of 9 th CGD Bidding Round, CGD would be \naccessible in 178 GAs covering approximately 280 districts spread over 26 States and UTs. \nPNGRB has also launched 10 th CGD bidding round.  After successful completion of 10 th CGD \nBidding Round, 70% of the country’s population would have access to CGD network. \n \n(b) & (c) Indraprastha Gas Limited (IGL) has been authorized to develop CGD netwo rk in Delhi \nwhich covers all the districts of Delhi . IGL has provided 6,6 1,243 domestic P iped Natural Gas \n(PNG) connections in Delhi . PNG connection is provided subject to pipeline connectivity and \nnecessary clearances received from different authorities.  \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_194": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 194 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nSHARADA PRASAD COMMITTEE REPORT \n \n194. DR. SHASHI THAROOR: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be pleased \nto state: \n \n(a)  whether the Government is aware that the Shara da Prasad Committee Report has held \nthat there is nepotism and irregularities in the working of sector skill councils;  \n(b)  if so, the details of the steps taken by the G overnment in relation to aforesaid findings; \n(c)  whether the Government is aware that the Shara da Prasad Committee Report has \nsuggested that to avoid conflict of interest, membe rs of National Skill Development Corporation \n(NSDC) should not be members of National Skill Deve lopment Funds (NSDF) and if so, the \ndetails thereof;  \n(d)  whether the Government has taken any steps to change the constitution of NSDF; and \n (e)  if so, the details thereof and if not, the re asons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI ANANTKUMAR HEGDE) \n \n(a) to (b)   The Government constituted a Committee  under Shri Sharda Prasad, former \nDirector General, Directorate General of Employment  & Training, Ministry of Labour & \nEmployment, Government of India, for rationalisatio n and optimization of the functioning of \nSector Skill Councils (SSCs), on 18.05 2016. \n \nThe Committee has made several recommendations on i nter alia, classification, role, \ngovernance structure and financing of SSCs. The Com mittee submitted its Report in December \n2016. The Report was placed in public domain and th ereafter there were three consultations \nheld at Bangalore (15th June, 2017), Mumbai (29th June, 2017) and Delhi (20th July, 2017) with \nall stakeholders viz SSCs, Industry Associations, S tate Governments, user industries, training \nproviders and Central Ministries/ Departments. Sinc e then NSDC has issued guidelines for \navoidance of conflict of interest in promoting organization of SSCs in August 2018. \n \n(c) to (e) The Cabinet in its meeting held on 28.03 .2018 had approved the proposal of \nMinistry Skill Development & Entrepreneurship (MSDE ) to revise composition of the Board of \nTrustees of National Skill Development Fund (NSDF).  The revised composition of Board of \nTrustees of NSDF is as under: \n \n(i) Secretary, MSDE \n(ii) Chief Executive Officer, National Institution for Transforming India (9NITI) Aayog \nor a nominee not below rank of Joint Secretary (JS); \n(iii) Secretary, Department of Financial Services o r a nominee not below the rank of \nJS: and  \n(iv) Representative from industry to be nominated b y Government of India \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_195": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 195 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nGENDER DISAGGREGATED DATA UNDER SKILL INDIA MISSION \n \n195. KUMARI SUSHMITA DEV: \n        \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)  the details of gender disaggregated data of th e number of people trained under the Skill \nIndia Mission from 2014 to 2018; State/ UT-wise including Assam; and  \n \n(b)  the details of gender disaggregated data of th e number of people who have received \nemployment after being trained under the Skill Indi a Mission from 2014 to 2018, State-wise \nincluding Assam?  \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI ANANTKUMAR HEGDE) \n \n(a) & (b) Under Skill India Mission, Ministry of Sk ill Development and Entrepreneurship is \nimplementing schemes for imparting employable skill s to the youth through short term and long \nterm training. The Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) is the flagship scheme of the \nMinistry providing short term training to the youth  through affiliated training partners/ training \ncentres. After successful implementation of the Sch eme in 2015-16, the scheme was re-\nlaunched in October, 2016 and it as PMKVY-2.0 (2016 -20). The scheme is implemented PAN \nIndia including Assam. State-wise, gender-wise deta ils of beneficiaries under PMKVY 1.0 and \nPMKVY 2.0 (2016-20) are at Annexure I, II and III, which includes the details for the state of \nAssam also. Long term training is imparted through Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs). The \nstate-wise and gender wise details of the trainees pass out from the ITIs, during the period \n2014-2018 are placed at Annexure IV. \n  \n  \n\nAnnexure I \nState wise details of beneficiaries under PMKVY 1.0 under short term training \n  \n \n  Female Male \nS.No. State Name T