    "ls|LS16_S17_U_205": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.†205 \nANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nDEVELOPMENT OF RURAL TOURISM \n \n†205. SHRI KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE:  \nSHRI M.B. RAJESH:  \nSHRIMATI REKHA VERMA:  \nSHRIMATI BHAVANA PUNDALIKRAO GAWALI PATIL:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether there is an immense potential for development of \nrural tourism in the country and if so, the details thereof;  \n(b)  whether the Government has formulated any scheme for the \npromotion of rural to urism in the country and if so, the details \nthereof along with the status of rural tourism projects \nimplemented/ sanctioned in this regard State/UT-wise;  \n(c)  whether the Government has received  any proposals from the \nStates/UTs in this regard and if so, the details thereof;  \n(d)  the number of villages identified and developed as rural tourist \nspots under rural tourism during the last three years and the \ncurrent year State/UT-wise; and  \n(e)  the details of funds allocated and expenditure incurred on \nsuch projects during the last three years and the current year, \nproject-wise and year-wise? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR TOURISM (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \n(SHRI K.J. ALPHONS) \n \n(a) to (e):  Rural tourism has been identified as one of the Niche \nTourism areas for dev elopment in the country by the Ministry of \nTourism.  \n \n\nUnder the Swadesh Darshan scheme, the Ministry is \ndeveloping theme - based tourism circuits in the country. Rural \nCircuit is one of the fifteen thematic circuits identified for \ndevelopment under the Scheme.  \n \nSubmission of project proposals by the State Governments/ \nUnion Territory (UT) Administrations under the Swadesh Darshan \nScheme is a continuous process. The projects for development \nunder the scheme are identified in consultation with the State \nGovernments/UT Administrations and are sanctioned subject to \navailability of funds, submission of suitable detailed project reports, \nadherence to scheme guidelines and utilization of funds released \nearlier. The details of the projects sanctioned by the Ministry  of \nTourism under the Rural Circuit theme are as below:     \n                                                                  (Rs. in crore)                                                                \n \nThe above projects are at different stages of implementation. \n \nFor the promotion of rural tourism in the country, the Ministry \nof Tourism undertakes several promotional activities in the \ndomestic and international mar kets. As part of its \nmarketing/promotional activities, the Ministry produces publicity \nmaterial and co llaterals in English and foreign languages and \nreleases print, electronic and online media campaigns in important \nand potential markets under the ‘Incredible India’ brand -line. \nPromotions are also undertaken through the website and social \nmedia accounts of the Ministry. \n \n******** \n \nSl. \nNo. \nState/Year \nof \nSanction \nName of the Project Amount \nSanctioned \nAmount \nReleased \n1. Bihar \n2017-18 \nDevelopment of \nBhitiharwa - Chandrahia - \nTurkaulia   \n44.65 8.93 \n2. Kerala \n2018-19 \nDevelopment of Malanad \nMalabar Cruise Tourism \n80.37 0.00 ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_206": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 206 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nSETTING UP OF DISPENSARY-CUM-BRANCH OFFICE \n  \n206. SHRI R. GOPALAKRISHNAN:  \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n  \n(a)whether the Government proposes to set up ESIC Dispensary -cum-\nBranch Office (DCBO) in every district and selected few districts of \nevery State for the purpose in the first phase; \n(b)if so, the details thereof and the present status of implementation of \nthe first phase; \n(c)the time by which these ESIC DCBO will be established; and  \n(d)the action taken/being taken by the Government to set up the ESIC \nDCBO in the remaining Districts, including Madurai District? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n(a):  Yes, Madam. Employees’ State Insurance Corporation (ESIC) has \ndecided to setup Dispensary -cum-Branch Office (DCBO) in every \ndistrict notified under ESIC Act and to begin with has selected a few \ndistricts in some of the States in the first phase. \n(b):  As of now 314 DCBOs have been sanctioned and out of which 29 \nDCBOs are made functional. The State -wise list of places/District \nwhere DCBOs have been sanctioned is attached as Annexure -I and \nthe list of places where 29 DCBOs are made functional in the first \nphase is attached as Annexure -II.  \nContd..2/- \n\n::  2  :: \n(c): Once the various factors like recruitment of Ministerial/Medical \nand Paramedical Staff, hiring of buildings and arrangement of basic \ninfrastructure in the office is completed, the DCBOs will star t \nfunctioning. The process of recruitment of manpower and arrangement \nof the other requirement is being done. \n(d): The ESI Corporation, under vision 2022 took a decision to extend \nthe coverage under ESI Act 1948, to all the districts in the country by \nthe year 2022 and also decided to setup at least one Dispensary –cum- \nBranch Office in each of the covered district , including Madurai by \n2022. \n \n**                                              ******* \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (b)  OF LOK SABHA UN -STARRED QUESTION \nNO. 206 FOR 04.02.2019 BY SHRI R. GOPALAKRISHNAN  REGARDING SETTING UP OF \nDISPENSARY-CUM-BRANCH OFFICE. \n \nSl No Name of Region Total No of DCBO Name of Places \n1 Jammu & Kashmir 4 \nKatra \nUdhampur \nSambha \nSrinagar \n2 Jharkhand 18 \nWest Singhbhum \nHazaribagh \nGarhwa \nPalamu \nLatehar \nLohardaga \nSimdega \nKhunti \nGumla \nChatra \nJamtara \nPakur \nGodda \nSahebganj \nDumka \nGhatshila \nChandil \nPatratu \n3 Haryana 8 \nKurukshetra \nJhajjar \nMahendergarh \nFatehabad \nKaithal \nFaridabad Sec 16 \nBahadurgarh \nMewat \n4 Karnataka 8 \nBidar \nChamarajanagar \nChikkaballapura \nHaveri \nKodaguru \nYadgir \nUttara Kannada (Karwar) \n\nChikkamagaluru \n5 Uttarakhand 4 \nSrinagar, Pauri Garhwal \nHaridwar \nRudrapur \nNew Tehri, Tehri Garhwal \n6 Uttar Pradesh 21 \nBhadoi, Sant Ravidas Nagar \nAmethi \nAmroha \nBijnaur \nChandauli \nEtawah \nFarrukhabad \nFatehpur \nGazipur \nHapur \nHardoi \nHathras \nKanpur Dehat \nMirzapur \nMuzaffarnagar \nRampur \nSant Kabeer Nagar \nShahjahanpur \nBareilly \nMoradabad \nSitapur \n7 Kerala 6 \nMunnar \nSulthan Bathery \nRanni \nBalussery \nThazhekode \nKanhangad \n8 Rajasthan 9 \nChhabda \nBoondi \nChuru \nKaroli \nSawai Madhopur \nPratapgarh \nChittorgarh \nJhunjhunu \nJalore \n9 West Bengal 8 Birbhum \nMurshidabad \n\nMalda \nJalpaiguri \nCoochbehar \nJhargram \nBankura \nFalta \n10 Telangana 18 \nAdilabad \nBibinagar \nJagtial \nJanagaon \nJaya Shankar Bhupalpally \nJogulamba Gadwal \nKamareddy \nKarimnagar \nKhammam \nNagarkurnool \nRajanna Sirisilla \nSuryapet \nWanaparthy \nWarangal Rural \nMedak \nRanga Reddy Dist. \nVikarabad \nMahabubabad \n11 Punjab 5 \nMuktsar \nNawanshahr \nDerabassi, Mohali \nBarnala \nRajpura \n12 Himachal 