    "ls|LS16_S17_U_45": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\n \nMINISTRY OF MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n \nLOK SABHA\n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 45\n \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019\n \n \nLEAN MANUFACTURING COMPETITIVENESS SCHEME\n \n \n45. \n \nSHRIMATI KIRRON KHER:\n \n \n(a)\n \nthe details of progress made under various \ncomponents of the Lean \nManufacturing Competitiveness Scheme for the period of 2014\n-\n18;\n \n(b)\n \nthe number of units that have been suspended from a Mini\n-\nCluster till date and \nthe reasons therefor;\n \n(c)\n \nthe details of performance parameters and targets that have been def\nined under \nthe said scheme; and \n \n(d)\n \nwhether before and after status reports have been prepared for all the identified \nclusters on the various parameters and if so, the details thereof along with the details \nof the number of clusters that have achieved the tim\ne bound targets for incremental \nimprovements?\n \n \n \nANSWER\n \n \nMINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE)\n \nFOR MICRO, SMALL AND MEDIUM ENTERPRISES\n \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH)\n \n \n \n(a):  \n \n478 Mini Clusters have been formed under the scheme during the period 2014\n-\n18.\n \n \n(b): \n \n238 \nunits are reported to have dropped out of the scheme at different stages of \nimplementation due to various reasons such as closure of the unit, change of business, \nother personal reasons, etc.\n \n \n(c)&(d): \n \nUnder the scheme, the Micro, Small and Medium Enterpr\nises are \nassisted with the target to reduce waste, better space utilization, reduction in \ninventory, improvement in productivity & process flow, timely delivery etc. Baseline \ndata and post implementation data are collected for units covered under the schem\ne. \nAs per the Independent Evaluation Study of the scheme, following outcomes have \nbeen reported: \n \n \n(i)\n \nEnhancement of productivity. \n \n(ii)\n \nReduction of waste.\n \n(iii)\n \nIncreased employee morale.\n \n(iv)\n \nReduction in transportation cost, improvement in inventory \nmanagement, etc.\n \n \n******\n \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_46": " \n \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 46 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2019 \n \nTuition Fees of IIMs \n \n46. DR. KIRIT SOMAIYA: \n \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether Government is planning to put a cap on the tuition fees of Indian Institutes \nof Management (IIMs) in the country;  \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n \n(c) whether the Government is incorporat ed a provision in the draft rules under new \nIIM Act to put a condition on the tuition fee charged by IIMs; \n \n(d) if so, whether IIMs Management have expressed concern about this provision; \n \n(e) if so, the details thereof; and \n \n(f) whether the Government would revisit the draft rules and alter this provision and if \nso, the reaction of the Government thereto? \n \nA N S W E R \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(DR. SATYA PAL SINGH) \n \n(a) to (f): The Indian Institute of Manageme nt Rules, 2018 has already been notified. \nThere is no provision for putting cap on tuition fees in the Rules.  \n \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS16_S17_U_47": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 47 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 4TH FEBRUARY, 2019 \n \nACTION PLAN FOR PROVIDING EMPLOYMENT \n \n47.   SHRI AJAY MISRA TENI: \n \n  Will the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether any action plans/schemes have been prepared/proposed to be prepared \nby the Government for providing employment to the unemployed persons during \nthe last three years and the current year; \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the number of per sons to whom employment \nhas been provided through  these plans/schemes during the period, plan/ scheme -\nwise and State/UT-wise; and \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE (IC) FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI SANTOSH KUMAR GANGWAR) \n \n(a) to (c): Employment generation coupled with improving employability is the priority \nconcern of the Government . Government has taken various steps for generating \nemployment in the country like encouraging private sector of economy, fast tracking \nvarious projects i nvolving substantial investment and increasing public expenditure \non schemes like Prime Minister’s Employment Generation Programme (PMEGP) run by \nMinistry of Micro, Small & Medium Enterprises, Mahatma Gandhi National Rural \nEmployment Guarantee Scheme (MGNR EGA), Pt. Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen \nKaushalya Yojana (DDU -GKY) scheme run by Ministry of Rural Development and \nDeendayal Antyodaya Yojana- National Urban Livelihoods Mission (DAY-NULM) run by \nMinistry of Housing & Urban Affairs. Details of the employmen t generated through \nthese schemes/ programmes are given at Annexure. \nPradhan Mantri Mudra Yojana (PMMY) has been initiated by Government for \nfacilitating self-employment. Under PMMY collateral free loans upto Rs. 10 lakh, are \nextended to small/micro busine ss enterprises and to individuals to enable them to \nsetup or expand their business activities. Till 25 th January, 2019, total 15.59 crore \nloans have been sanctioned under the scheme. \n \nPradhan Mantri Rojgar Protsahan Yojana has been initiated by the Ministr y of Labour \nand Employment in the year 2016 -17 for incentivizing employers for employment \ngeneration. Under this scheme, Government is paying the entire employer’s \ncontribution (12 % or as admissible) towards the EPS and EPF for all sectors w.e.f. \n01.04.2018  to all eligible new employees for the next 3 years from the date of \nregistration of the new employee. Till 28th January, 2019, benefits have been given to \n1.29 lakh establishments covering 1.05 crore beneficiaries. \n*****  \n\nAnnexure \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (c) OF THE LOK  SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 47 FOR 04.02.2019 REGARDING ACTION PLAN FOR PROVIDING EMPLOYMENT \n(a) Year –wise /State-wise details of  Prime Minister’s Employment Genaration Programme (PMEGP)  \nSl. No.  State   \n2015-16 2016-17 2017-18 2018-19 \n(As on 30.11.2018) \n1 Andaman & Nicobar Islands 293 1398                    \n1744 1064 \n2 Andhra Pradesh 7740 14148 12216 9008 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh 104 1984 1672 1496 \n4 Assam 9026 31498 18256 16424 \n5 Bihar 19624 25872 18456 10776 \n6 Chandigarh 323 376 360 128 \n7 Chhattisgarh 9496 12856 11704 11792 \n8 Delhi 2048 952 920 384 \n9 Goa 500 660 400 232 \n10 Gujarat* 14960 11629 15008 14488 \n11 Haryana 7232 11016 13744 8024 \n12 Himachal Pradesh 5134 6916 7088 5528 \n13 Jammu and Kashmir 12115 11691 30024 27752 \n14 Jharkhand 12873 10400 8888 4472 \n15 Karnataka 17284 30286 16920 15360 \n16 Kerala 9653 13068 10776 9520 \n17 Lakshadweep - - - - \n18 Madhya Pradesh 16497 15520 14432 8040 \n19 Maharashtra** 20161 17799 26632 21960 \n20 Manipur 2715 8419 4800 4680 \n21 Meghalaya 4824 2632 600 1472 \n22 Mizoram 9072 3400 1992 3336 \n23 Nagaland 4998 7783 7440 3296 \n24 Odisha 17629 20392 19192 11808 \n25 Puducherry                                                                        